      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those feelings of emptiness despite having good things going on can be incredibly isolating and confusing, especially when it feels like you do everything \"right.\" This experience might be a sign of depression, which doesn't always have a single obvious cause but instead manifests as a persistent fog that drains your energy and joy. Please consider reaching out to a mental health professional who can help you explore these emotions without judgment, as they specialize in navigating this kind of internal weight. You deserve support to help you see through that gray fog again, and taking that first step to talk to someone is a powerful move toward healing.",
