      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly brave of you to share that previous therapy didn't resolve the fog for you, as feeling hopeless despite treatment is a very common experience that requires a different approach. Please know that your worth isn't defined by your functionality, and giving up on talking to someone is rarely a failure, even if it feels like the only available option. Reaching out to a crisis line or a specialized provider who listens without trying to \"fix\" you immediately might provide a safe space simply for venting, even if the noise doesn't quiet right away. There is still hope that a different perspective or connection can offer relief, even if it feels distant right now.",
